#!/usr/bin/env python3
# apply_live_exit_fixes_20261027.py — Scalp App live-exit hardening + end-to-end
# strategy tests, one file. SUPERSEDES apply_live_exit_fixes_20261026.py: run
# it on untouched v11.4.0, on v11.4.0 + the TMA-only patch, or on top of the
# 20261026 script. --revert always returns to v11.4.0.
#
# WHAT IT CHANGES (details: docs/INCIDENT_2026-10-26_TMA_EXIT.md, written by
# this script):
#   * ExecutionRouter forwards place_gtt_sl_only_short/long,
#     place_gtt_tp_only_long and get_basket_margin. These were missing since
#     2026-08-18, so TMA/IC SL GTTs were never placed and the margin guard
#     silently skipped.
#   * TMA_V1, TMA_V2, IC_V1/V2, VET_V1 and TSG_V1 LIVE exits are driven to a
#     CONFIRMED fill: re-peg, cancel on timeout, confirm. Nothing is booked
#     unless it filled. The hedge is sold only after its short is flat.
#     Stuck exits retry and page.
#   * VET_V1: LIVE trade rows now save (tuple order-id bug); entries are
#     fill-confirmed.
#   * Tests: incident replays for every strategy, a router contract scan,
#     and END-TO-END suites (TMA_V2 15 flows, IC_V2 11, VET_V1 9, TSG_V1 8)
#     through the real ExecutionRouter over a Kite-shaped fake broker. Tests
#     are hermetic: they never touch your real app.db, Telegram or audit log.
#
# USAGE (from the repo root, the folder containing backend/; or pass --repo):
#   python3 apply_live_exit_fixes_20261027.py --dry-run   # check only
#   python3 apply_live_exit_fixes_20261026.py             # apply + run tests
#   python3 apply_live_exit_fixes_20261027.py --revert    # undo THIS script
#
# SAFETY: every target file is checksum-verified against v11.4.0 (or v11.4.0
# plus the TMA patch, or v11.4.1 = the 20261026 script). If ANY file
# differs, NOTHING is written. Pre-existing versions are kept as
# <file>.bak-LIVE_EXIT_E2E_20261027 (house convention); --revert restores
# exactly what you had before running this script. Restart the backend.
